From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wangzlei <66336933+wangzlei@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:22:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] autoname: service name from project metadata / command
 line

A process without OTEL_SERVICE_NAME (or service.name in
OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES), without a discovery criteria name and without
Kubernetes metadata is named after its executable: python3, node, dotnet,
java. Several services on one host then share one name, and patch 01
propagates that useless name to their callers as peer.service.name.

With discovery.service_name_from_cmdline: true (env
OTEL_EBPF_SERVICE_NAME_FROM_CMDLINE), the trace attacher derives a name before
the process is instrumented (attacher.go resolveServiceMetadata, which runs
before getTracer -> monitorPIDs -> AllowPID), so it is also the name the
tpinjector writes into svc_name_by_pid and sends in the TCP option:

1. Project metadata, read inside /proc/<pid>/root (openat2 RESOLVE_IN_ROOT):
   - Node.js: package.json "name" from the script's directory up to the
     working directory, npm scope removed (@acme/orders-api -> orders-api);
     for a tool under node_modules (npm, next) only the working directory.
   - Python: [project].name (or [tool.poetry].name) of ./pyproject.toml.
   - Java (jvmtools, after spring.application.name and Implementation-Title):
     JAR name without its version (order-service-1.4.2.jar -> order-service),
     Start-Class behind a Spring Boot JarLauncher / WarLauncher /
     PropertiesLauncher (also the exploded /app/META-INF/MANIFEST.MF layout),
     else the main class's simple name (-cp/-p/--add-opens values, -D, -X,
     -javaagent skipped; -m module/Main -> Main).
   - .NET: dotnet X.dll -> X.
2. The entry argument, only for python*, node, ruby, php* (native binaries keep
   their executable name): the Python script, the last non-generic component
   of -m X, or the module of a gunicorn / uvicorn / hypercorn / waitress /
   daphne / celery target (also the setproctitle "gunicorn: worker [m:app]"
   form); the Node.js script (node options skipped); the Ruby / PHP script.
3. Never worse than before: names are sanitised to [A-Za-z0-9._-], a trailing
   -1.2.3 / -SNAPSHOT version is stripped, the length is capped at 63, and a
   generic result (main, app, index, server, run, start, wsgi, asgi, manage,
   application, dist, src, bin, lib, build; case-insensitive) or an empty one
   keeps the executable-name fallback (Java: the upstream JAR name).

The name is stored as an automatic name, so Kubernetes metadata still replaces
it, and environment / criteria names are never touched. ExecutableName() is
unchanged (it also labels OBI's internal metrics).

Why upstream does not do it: OBI names services from explicit configuration
(env, criteria, Kubernetes) and treats the executable name as a placeholder;
only Java has a resolver. Guessing names from command lines is a policy
choice, so it is opt-in here too.

Turn it off: discovery.service_name_from_cmdline: false (the default in code)
or OTEL_EBPF_SERVICE_NAME_FROM_CMDLINE=false. The adot-obi default configs
(config/otel.yaml, cwagent etc/ebpf) enable it.

Adot-Obi-Patch: 05-autoname
